        "original_id": "26885014-c3e6-5920-bd76-291e70650637",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elliot Goldenthal, Julie Taymor\n- Works: Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass, Frida\n- Awards: Obie Award, Academy Award for Best Original Score\n\nFacts:\n- Elliot Goldenthal was born on May 2, 1954, and he is an American composer of film scores and contemporary classical music.\n- Elliot Goldenthal first composed the Obie Award-winning score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass around 1988, when the musical opened off-Broadway in a small former church.\n- The score for Juan Darién: A Carnival Mass was later reworked and refined for the show's on-Broadway release in 1996.\n- Elliot Goldenthal won the Academy Award for Best Original Score in 2002 for his score for the film Frida.\n- Julie Taymor directed Frida and was Elliot Goldenthal's long-time partner.",
